# M4.24 static guard — local shell mismatch

Date: 2026-08-28

## Failure

The local reproduction of the M4.24 CI static guard was initially launched by
the macOS task shell (`zsh`). The workflow step itself declares `shell: bash`,
but the local wrapper did not. `zsh` reserves the variable name `status`, so the
wrapper stopped with `read-only variable: status` before YAML validation.

The repeated Bash guard passed. The separate optional Python YAML parser probe
then found that PyYAML is not installed on this Mac. This does not affect GitHub
Actions or the repository test suite; YAML syntax is repeated with the system
Ruby/Psych parser instead of installing a new dependency during review.

## Cause and impact

This is a local test-harness shell mismatch, not a workflow failure. No service,
server, provider, contract or repository history was changed. The full Python
regression had already passed 182 tests.

## Minimal correction

Repeat the unchanged workflow guard with `/bin/bash` explicitly, retain the
workflow's declared Bash shell, and use the already installed system YAML
parser for the local syntax-only check.

## Rollback

No runtime rollback is applicable. The uncommitted review can still be removed
to return to `758b404d5fe69b5395ff6e73cd3542b6da141926`.
